  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "description": "<div>\n  <p>A journey from the top-left to bottom-right cell uses side-adjacent steps. Its effort is the greatest absolute height change on any single step. Return the smallest achievable effort, not the sum of changes.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> heights = [[1,2,2],[3,8,2],[5,3,5]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2</pre>\n  <p>A route avoiding the large central jump achieves maximum difference two.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> heights = [[1,2,3],[3,8,4],[5,3,5]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1</pre>\n  <p>A winding route can keep every step within one unit.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> heights = [[7]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre>\n  <p>No step is needed.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>1 &lt;= rows, columns &lt;= 100</code>; all rows have equal length.</li>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= heights[r][c] &lt;= 1000000</code>.</li>\n    <li>A one-cell path has effort <code>0</code>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
  "templates": {
    "python": "class Solution:\n    def minimumEffortPath(self, heights: List[List[int]]):\n        \"\"\"NUMBER\"\"\"\n        pass\n",
    "javascript": "class Solution {\n  /** Return the required number result. */\n  minimumEffortPath(heights) {\n    // your code here\n  }\n}\n"
  },
